  "text": "Pieper Veterinary | 24/7 Emergency, Urgent Care & Specialty Hospital in Connecticut\nPieper Veterinary | 24/7 Emergency, Urgent Care & Specialty Hospital in Connecticut\nClose\nEmergency Services\nVisiting the ER\nUrgent Care\nStray Pets & Wildlife\nSpecialty Services\nAvian & Exotics\nClinical Pathology\nCritical Care\nDiagnostic Imaging\nInternal Medicine\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOncology\nSurgery\nPrimary Care\nWellness Plans\nWellness Exams\nSick Visits\nVaccinations\nSpay/Neuter Surgery\nGeneral Surgery\nDentistry\nFlea/Tick Prevention\nPuppy & Kitten Care\nLocations\nPieper Memorial Veterinary Center\nPieper Veterinary Madison\nMarlborough Animal Hospital\nPieper Veterinary Berlin Street\nEssex Veterinary Clinic\nPieper Veterinary Stratford and Referral Center\nLebanon Veterinary Hospital\nElm City Vet\nMountain Lore Animal Hospital\nNorwichtown Veterinary Hospital\nAbout Us\nOur History\nMeet Our Doctors\nContinuing Education\nVeterinary Technology Program\nVeterinary Internship, Residency and Externship Programs\nResources\nBlog\nFor New Clients\nOur Store & RX Refill\nPayment\nPieper Olson Foundation\nJoin Our Team\nMessage Your Care Team\nReferring Vets\nBook Now\nOnline Store\nEmergency Services\nVisiting the ER\nUrgent Care\nStray Pets & Wildlife\nSpecialty Services\nAvian & Exotics\nClinical Pathology\nCritical Care\nDiagnostic Imaging\nInternal Medicine\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOncology\nSurgery\nPrimary Care\nWellness Plans\nWellness Exams\nSick Visits\nVaccinations\nSpay/Neuter Surgery\nGeneral Surgery\nDentistry\nFlea/Tick Prevention\nPuppy & Kitten Care\nLocations\nPieper Memorial Veterinary Center\nPieper Veterinary Madison\nMarlborough Animal Hospital\nPieper Veterinary Berlin Street\nEssex Veterinary Clinic\nPieper Veterinary Stratford and Referral Center\nLebanon Veterinary Hospital\nElm City Vet\nMountain Lore Animal Hospital\nNorwichtown Veterinary Hospital\nAbout Us\nOur History\nMeet Our Doctors\nContinuing Education\nVeterinary Technology Program\nVeterinary Internship, Residency and Externship Programs\nResources\nBlog\nFor New Clients\nOur Store & RX Refill\nPayment\nPieper Olson Foundation\nJoin Our Team\nMessage Your Care Team\nReferring Vets\nBook Now\nOnline Store\nYour browser does not support the HTML5 video tag.\nComprehensive Veterinary Care Across Connecticut\nPrimary, emergency, and specialty veterinary care across Connecticut. Our hospitals keep pets healthy and supported at every step.\nPrimary\nCare\nFor preventative care and wellness\nBook an Appointment\nFind a Location\nER and\nSpecialty Care\nSerious illness, injury, or complex conditions\nGet Care Now\nFind a Location\nYour browser does not support the HTML5 video tag.\nComprehensive Veterinary Care Across Connecticut\nPrimary, emergency, and specialty veterinary care across Connecticut. Our hospitals keep pets healthy and supported at every step.\nPrimary\nCare\nFor preventative care and wellness\nBook an Appointment\nFind a Location\nER and\nSpecialty Care\nSerious illness, injury, or complex conditions\nGet Care Now\nFind a Location\nTrusted Veterinary Care for Connecticut Pets\nConnected Care at Every Step\nOur locations work together so your pet’s medical history moves with them, whether it's a routine check-up or an emergency.\nExplore Our Locations\nTop-Tier Clinical Care\n100+ veterinarians, including specialists in oncology, neurology, and more, deliver cutting-edge care.\nMeet Our Team\nServing Connecticut with Heart\nOver 80 years of compassionate, personalized care for pets and their owners.\nOur Story\nMillions Cared For. One Tail at a Time.\nCare That Doesn’t Clock Out—We’re Open Evenings and Weekends.\nPrimary Care\nWellness, vaccinations, routine surgery and dentistry for your pet’s lifelong health.\nLearn More\nSpecialty Care\nAdvanced treatments in oncology, neurology, and exotic pet care.\nLearn More\n24/7 Emergency Care\nImmediate help for trauma, toxins, or critical conditions at our ERs.\nLearn More\n“Everyone, the front desk staff, vet techs, doctors, took the time we needed to help us understand what was happening and what steps would be taken. I tell anyone who will listen about Pieper, you're the best!”\nWendy C\n“The staff was extremely compassionate, professional, and knowledgeable during a very difficult time…  I had to drive over an hour to get to Pieper and I will tell you that I would drive that again to bring my animal here for top notch care.”\nMicaela O.\n“Dr Urbonas was everything you hope a doctor would be in an urgent medical situation - professional and knowledgeable, kind and caring, confident and positive. With a reassuring \"we got this\" attitude.”\nMaryann M.\n“Thanks to their expertise and unwavering care, our girl is back home, healing, and slowly returning to her joyful self. We are forever grateful.”\nNicole S.\n“Everyone is so kind and helpful! I love how down to earth the staff members are. I'm so grateful to have such a wonderful team working with me and my pets!”\nAutumn S.\n“Pieper made my dog and I feel so welcome and taken care of the whole time we were there. 10/10, fantastic care.”\nAnnabelle M.\n“The front desk staff celebrating with me when I shared the news that [my cat] was okay is something I will never forget. Every step of the process, I knew I could trust Pieper to deliver the best veterinary care and owner support.”\nMax S.\n“The techs and veterinarians were incredibly kind and efficient. I have nothing but good things to say about this place and I am so grateful that they took care of our dog the way they did.”\nJoey A.\n“Every single member of the staff cared greatly about the pets that were there. Outstanding communication, both written and verbal, and did a wonderful job at managing expectations.”\nJon S.\n“Dr. Carreras and her Pieper Oncology Team go above and beyond. The care, empathy, communication and overall professionalism they all provide is amazing.”\nTed W.\n“Thanks to all who helped Gus thru his surgery and recovery, especially Dr Heather Mossman and everyone who attended to Gus during his stay. You set my family at ease knowing our sweet boy Gus was in the best of hands.”\nRichard D.\n“Pieper has the best veterinary staff that have ever treated my pets in all my experience as a pet owner.”\nSavannah S.\n“We had a fantastic experience. The entire team took great care of Henry and kept us updated the entire time. He is doing great and we are so thankful!”\nVeronica F.\n“The genuine care from every single staff member just blows my mind. I can't speak highly enough of every single person associated with Pieper. Thank you for all you have done for me and my Mochi.”\nJamie P.\n“My rabbit and I had a great appointment with the exotics department! It's a relief to have a specialist nearby that is knowledgeable, experienced, and comfortable with protocols to keep stress as low as possible.”\nCara S.\n“Extraordinary service and care. I am a nurse. I pay attention to the details. Pieper has hit it out of the park”\nFrances M.\n“I feel like my baby is in the best hands when it comes to the care he's receiving. Dr. Hammond is hands down the best doctor I've encountered!”\nKassandra J.\n“The staff at Pieper were very caring and professional. The Vets in Internal Medicine and Oncology were extremely knowledgeable and thorough. I would highly recommend them”\nKen H.\nFind Your Nearest Pieper Veterinary\nWith several locations across Connecticut, expert care is close by.\nBook Appointment\nView All Locations\nMeet the Humans Your Pet Loves\nSit. Stay. Subscribe.\nMonthly pet care tips and updates, minus the fluff.\nFirst Name\n*\nLast Name\n*\nEmail\n*\nSubscribe\nVisiting The ER\nA guide of when to seek care.\nLearn More\nNew Client Info\nForms and what to expect.\nGet Started\nrDVM Resources\nReferral guides and specialist contacts.\nExplore\nPet Education\nPet care blogs and more.\nRead Blog\nJoin Our Team\nResources\nReferring Vets\nMessage Us\nEmergency & Specialty Car